  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1258 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nWidespread showers are expected to continue this morning. Some \ngusty winds upwards of 30 mph may still be possible as these \nstorms move through. Cloudy skies will persist through the early\nafternoon today and will begin to break during the late \nafternoon and evening. With some clearing temperatures will \nreach the mid to upper 60s across the region today. Skies will \nclear out almost completely Wednesday night allowing for \nanother mild, sunny day Thursday. \n\nA positively tilted trough and associated cold front is \nforecast for Friday morning. At this time, no rain is \nanticipated with the arrival of this front. Highs will cool off \nto the upper 50s and low 60s Friday and through the weekend \nbefore warming back up into the mid 60s to low 70s by mid next \nweek. Low temperatures will drop as well with lows in the upper\n30s Friday night and low to mid 30s Saturday and Sunday night.",
